12345 Spareribs
  --Ming-Na Wen

1 1/2 lb pork spareribs, uncooked and cut into 2" bone-in pieces
2 tbsp Shaoxing Chinese cooking wine
6 tbsp Chinkiang vinegar (or rice vinegar)
4 tbsp light shoyu
1/2 c sugar

Fill a large pot with water and bring it to a boil. Add the spareribs to blanch the meat and cook for ~4 min. Drain and discard the water. Rinse the cooked ribs and return them to the pot. Turn the heat to medium-high and add the cooking wine, vinegar, shoyu, sugar, and 3/4 c water, stirring to dissolve the sugar. Bring it to a boil. Lower the heat to medium-low, cover, and simmer gently until the meat is tender, 45 min to 1 hr, turning the ribs occasionally. Remove the cover and bring the remaining liquid to a full Stir until the water is mostly evaporated and only a shiny sauce is left on the ribs, ~5 min. Serve hot!
